[FABRICATED] 2012-06-03-the-jubilation-of-spring.md  (3 body lines not found in source)
    The event takes place at 3 p.m., June 3, St. Paul's United Church, 29 Park St. W., Dundas.
    Music director Laura Thomas will lead the orchestra in a program featuring music written about and for springtime. The concert will include music by Canadian composer Alice Ho and Robert Schumann's Symphony No. 1. Also on the program will be On Hearing the First Cuckoo of Spring by Delius, Sibelius' Spring Song and The Voices of Spring by Johann Strauss, Jr.
    The Dundas Valley Orchestra recently performed with many of Mohawk College's talented students at the annual music department Concerto Competition concert. Two of the soloists have been invited to perform again with the DVO on June 3. Violinists Marina Mulligan and Calypso McKnight will play the first movement of Mozart's Concertone for Two Violins. Both young musicians are students of Sonia Vizante.

[FABRICATED] 2013-01-20-songs-of-the-people.md  (6 body lines not found in source)
    The concert begins at 3 pm.
    Cello soloist  Stephanie Kim will be performing the Kol Nidrei by Max Bruch. Kim is a talented music student from the Niagara area.
    The program will also feature Rimsky-Korsakov’s Symphony No. 1, Vaughan-Williams English Folk Song Suite, Butterworth’s On the Banks of Green Willow, Harry Somers’ Little Suite (on French Canadian Themes) for String Orchestra, and Claude Champagne’s Danse Villageoise.
    Many concert goers happily make donations of $10 or more, which will be acknowledged with a tax receipt. But as always, a donation is optional. The concert is provided free of charge.
    There is a reception following the concert. Mingle with the musicians over a coffee and a snack.
    See writeup in Greater Hamilton Musician: [Dundas Valley Orchestra's "Songs of the People" Concert Sunday January 20th](http://musicbizbites.blogspot.com/2013/01/dundas-valley-orchestras-songs-of.html)

